INT. HOLLOWAY KITCHEN - NIGHT

Pitch black. A candle FLARES to life. Behind it DENISE HOLLOWAY, 40s, holds a lighter and a very large frozen turkey in the crook of one arm. At the island GAIL PRUITT, 50s, her sister-in-law, squints at a dead tablet. The fridge hums its last breath and stops.

DENISE
Okay. Nobody panic. The turkey has eleven hours of cold left in it.

GAIL
It's a bird Denise not a battery.

CLOSE ON the oven clock. Blinking nothing. Dead.

ANGLE ON the back door. It opens and DR. RAJ MEHTA, 50s, neighbour and a gastroenterologist, steps in holding a head torch and a casserole dish he has clearly been carrying out of habit.

RAJ
Whole street is out. Transformer. I've triaged the Hendersons they're stable but the Hendersons are always stable.

DENISE
Raj you can't just walk in.

RAJ
Door was open. Clinically speaking that's an invitation.

Gail stands to hug Denise and knocks the candle which tips toward a stack of the takeaway menus and Denise lunges with the turkey while Raj swings the torch beam across the room catching the cat on top of the cupboard and the cat leaps and lands in the sink and the tap goes off like a gun because the pressure pump has died.

WE SEE the flame lick the first menu.

DENISE
Fire fire fire

GAIL
Smother it!

DENISE
With what

Gail points at the turkey. Denise looks at the turkey. Raj is already pouring the casserole's sauce over the flame, which hisses out. Silence. Smoke curls.

DENISE (CONT'D)
That was lasagne.

RAJ
It was a sacrifice.

INSERT - the charred menu, "Golden Wok" still legible.

BACK TO SCENE

Gail sits heavily. Denise sits beside her. Raj stays standing, torch under his chin like a campfire storyteller.

DENISE
She said she'd call about Christmas.

GAIL
I was going to say that.
^
DENISE
Also thanks for the lasagne.

RAJ
(to the dark)
Seventeen years of practice and I have never once saved a menu.

The lights come ON. Fridge shudders. Oven clock flashes 12:00. They all look up at it like a miracle.

GAIL
Well.

DENISE
Well.

The turkey, forgotten, slides out of her arm and hits the floor with a THUD.
